schema: "0.4"
id: npl-prism-29-reviews-list
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo collaboration — Reviews List: org-scoped listing of overlay-
# annotated screenshot reviews; entry point to start a new review.
# Theme tenets: luminous frosted glass, cool violet→cyan spectrum gradient, Sora
# geometric type, 16px radius; the review table stays on a solid legible surface.
# Palette: violet #7c3aed, cyan #06b6d4, fuchsia #d946ef, canvas #f7f8ff, ink #1a1730.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    PREMIUM review-management list inside a modern AI product. Polished and composed.
    A frosted-glass page chrome floats over a pale spectrum mesh; the primary "Create
    review" action carries the signature violet→cyan gradient; the review table itself
    sits on a solid, legible surface. Clean geometric sans-serif (Sora), no serif.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the REVIEWS LIST screen of NoizuPromptLingo
    (route /app/[orgId]/reviews).

    OVERALL LAYOUT (two bands): a slim LEFT app nav rail (achromatic glass) and a
    dominant CENTER content column — over a pale near-white canvas (#f7f8ff) with a soft
    blurred violet/cyan spectrum mesh glowing behind a frosted page header.

    HEADER BAND (frosted glass): "Reviews" title in Sora 700 with an org breadcrumb; a
    REVIEW STATUS FILTER as a row of pill chips ("All", "Open", "Compiled") with the
    active chip carrying a soft violet fill; and a primary CREATE REVIEW BUTTON
    (violet→cyan gradient, soft glow, "＋ New review") at the right that starts a review
    by uploading/selecting a screenshot.

    REVIEW TABLE (center, the focus): a card with a frosted glass frame but a SOLID
    opaque table body for legibility. Columns: Review (title) / Status / Reviewer /
    Target / Updated. Each row shows a small TARGET SCREENSHOT THUMBNAIL (a rounded
    mini-image of a UI screen) at left, a title, a STATUS chip — "Open" (flat cyan/blue)
    or "Compiled" (flat emerald #10b981), opaque never gradient — a reviewer avatar dot
    + name, and a muted timestamp. Show ~6 rows, quiet hairline rules, one row with a
    faint hover highlight and a small right-aligned kebab action revealed.

    An empty-state hint is NOT needed — the list is populated.

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool near-white canvas + soft spectrum mesh behind the frosted
    header; ink #1a1730 text; the violet(#7c3aed)→cyan(#06b6d4) gradient only on the
    Create Review button and the active filter/edge accents; status chips flat opaque.
    Sora everywhere, no serif.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: 16px radius on the header/card, pill filter chips, translucent
    frosted chrome with gradient-sheen edges — but the table body is a solid opaque
    surface. Violet-tinted soft shadow under the card; luminous, premium.

    MOOD: premium, organized, calm. A review queue that looks modern and inviting while
    keeping its data rows crisply legible.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, gradient body text, gradient status chips, rainbow tie-dye buttons, a data table rendered as unreadable translucent glass, neon-on-black cyberpunk"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches key components — Review Table with status/reviewer/target screenshot thumbnail, Create Review Button, Review Status Filter chips"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Prism frosted glass chrome over a spectrum mesh, violet→cyan gradient on primary action/active-filter only, flat opaque status chips, Sora type, 16px radius; table body on a solid legible surface"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear list hierarchy, scannable rows with thumbnails, plausible real-product layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, legible table text, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "the review data table rendered as low-legibility translucent glass"
    - "gradient status chips, gradient body text, or rainbow chrome"

tags: [npl-prism, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup, collaboration]
